From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Nov 2026 23:10:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ddraw: Update the window present rect on display mode changes.

When the cooperative level makes the window exclusive fullscreen, wined3d
sets its present rect to the desktop rect, and win32u maps the window to the
monitor with it. ddraw then changes the display mode separately and only
resizes the window, so the present rect still covered the old mode. After a
3840x2160 desktop switched to 800x600, the window visible rect became
(0,0)-(14304,7776): the stale 3840x2160 rect scaled 3.6 times for the new mode
and offset by the pillarbox.

On Wine-Wayland this created a 14336x7808 window surface that spilled onto
the next output. Star Wars Galactic Battlegrounds then lost keyboard focus
and its display mode, and quit with "Could not initialize graphics system".

Set the present rect to the new desktop rect before resizing the window, as
wined3d does for its own fullscreen mode changes.
---

--- a/dlls/ddraw/ddraw.c
+++ b/dlls/ddraw/ddraw.c
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 #include "d3dhal.h"
 
 #include "wine/exception.h"
+#include "ddk/d3dkmthk.h"
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(ddraw);
 
@@ -5091,6 +5092,25 @@
     TRACE("device_parent %p, device %p.\n", device_parent, device);
 }
 
+/* Exclusive fullscreen windows have a present rect, which win32u uses to map
+ * them to the monitor. wined3d sets it to the desktop rect when the window
+ * becomes fullscreen, and updates it on its own mode changes; ddraw changes
+ * the mode separately, so update it here, or the window keeps the size of the
+ * previous mode and gets scaled with the new one (e.g. a 3840x2160 present
+ * rect scaled 3.6x for an 800x600 mode). */
+static void ddraw_set_window_present_rect(HWND window, const RECT *rect)
+{
+    D3DKMT_ESCAPE escape = {0};
+    RECT present_rect = *rect;
+
+    escape.Type = D3DKMT_ESCAPE_SET_PRESENT_RECT_WINE;
+    escape.hContext = HandleToULong(window);
+    escape.pPrivateDriverData = &present_rect;
+    escape.PrivateDriverDataSize = sizeof(present_rect);
+    if (D3DKMTEscape(&escape))
+        WARN("Failed to set the present rect of window %p.\n", window);
+}
+
 /* This is run from device_process_message() in wined3d, we can't take the
  * wined3d mutex. */
 /* FIXME: We only get mode change notifications in exclusive mode, but we
@@ -5118,6 +5138,10 @@
     r = &output_desc.desktop_rect;
     TRACE("Resizing window %p to %s.\n", ddraw->swapchain_window, wine_dbgstr_rect(r));
 
+    /* Before resizing: win32u maps the window with its present rect. */
+    if (!ddraw->gf_overlay_window)
+        ddraw_set_window_present_rect(ddraw->swapchain_window, r);
+
     /* The temporary video window is not the fullscreen device window. */
     if (!ddraw->gf_overlay_window
             && !SetWindowPos(ddraw->swapchain_window, HWND_TOP, r->left, r->top,
-- 
